larkbox-fan - fan control for Chuwi LarkBox (Celeron J4115) on Linux

The LarkBox BIOS switches its 2-wire fan inside the ACPI method
\_SB.SEN4._TMP (DPTF temperature sensor "Thermistor Skin", INT3403):
if the CPU package temperature is above 55 C it drives a GPIO high
(fan on), otherwise low (fan off). The method only runs when something
reads the SEN4 temperature. Windows' Intel DPTF service polls it every
few seconds; Linux never does, so the fan gets stuck in its last state.

This package installs a tiny systemd service that reads
/sys/class/thermal/thermal_zoneN/temp of the SEN4 zone every 5 seconds.
The firmware then switches the fan exactly like on Windows.

The service only starts on machines whose SMBIOS product name starts
with "LarkBox", and exits quietly if no SEN4 thermal zone exists.

Check:   systemctl status larkbox-fan
Logs:    journalctl -u larkbox-fan
Interval: systemctl edit larkbox-fan, then add
          [Service]
          Environment=LARKBOX_FAN_INTERVAL=2

Project page: https://github.com/lmnikolaev/larkbox-fan
